>> title: Pad Thai
>> category: Noodles
>> tags: noodles, shrimp, thai, tamarind, wok
>> counters: Thai Kitchen
>> aka: phat thai, phad thai, pad thai goong, pad thai kung, thai fried noodles, pad thai noodles
>> pairs-with: pad-thai-sauce
>> servings: 2
>> time: 45 min
>> step.1: soak 30 min, drain
>> step.2: fry 2 min
>> step.3: stir-fry 3 min
>> step.4: scramble in
>> step.5: toss off the heat

Soak @dried rice stick noodles{6%oz}(170 g; 3 mm wide) in warm water for ~soak{30%min}, until they are bendy but still chalky at the centre, then drain them. They finish cooking in the wok, and noodles boiled soft first turn to paste there.

Fry @dried shrimp{2%Tbs}(rinsed), @preserved radish{2%Tbs}(chopped; chai poh), @firm tofu{4%oz}(115 g; in 1/2-in cubes) and @garlic{3%cloves}(chopped) in @vegetable oil{3%Tbs} in a hot #wok{} for ~fry{2%min}, until the tofu takes some colour.

Stir-fry @&(~2)drained noodles{} into @&(~1)aromatics{} with @pad thai sauce{1/3%cup}(80 mL) and @large shrimp{8}(peeled, tails on) over the highest heat you have for ~stirfry{3%min}, turning rather than stirring, until the noodles drink the sauce and go glossy.

Push @&(~1)noodles{} to one side, break @eggs{2%large} into the bare metal, let them set for a count of ten, then chop them through.

Toss @&(~1)noodles{} off the heat with @bean sprouts{1%cup}(a big handful), @garlic chives{4}(in 2-in lengths), @roasted peanuts{3%Tbs}(coarsely crushed), @lime{1}(in wedges) and @toasted chile powder{1%tsp}, which each eater adds to their own plate.
